From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thelamer <ryankuba@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:35:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] vp9: Copy only the source blocks the active map leaves
 active

A pushed frame is copied whole into a lookahead buffer, and extended, whatever the active map
says; a screen encoder marks most of its blocks inactive on most frames, and the copy is the same
size as the picture. Each lookahead buffer now records, per 16x16 block, whether the picture
changed since the buffer last held it (the active blocks of every push since), and a push with
an active map copies the blocks the map leaves active and those that changed since, through a
rectangle copy that extends the border where a rectangle ends at the picture's edge. A frame
without a map, with a forced key frame, resized, or in high bit depth is copied whole and marks
every block of the other buffers changed.

The stream comes out bit for bit the same as with the whole copy, at 1920x1080, 2560x1600 and
1366x768, constant quantizer and constant rate, one and eight threads, on a still screen, a
256x256 changing box and a scroll.
